<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayyida Shirin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1028</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sayyida Shirin was a Buyid queen who ruled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rayy">Rayy</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> as regent for her son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majd-al-dawla">Majd al-Dawla</a> from 997 until her death in 1028. A princess of the Bavandid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, she kept power by skilful diplomacy, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> is said to have held back from attacking while she lived. He took Rayy in 1029, the year after her death.</p></div>
